window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-81de09346a07fee6"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"set-up-and-manage-teams-and-team-tasks\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">设置和管理团队与团队任务</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 中的团队为成员提供共同组织工作和协作的空间。借助团队任务，成员可以设置定时工作，或在特定事件发生时运行工作，例如准备每周报告或汇总新的项目进展。</p> <p>开始使用前，请先了解如何<a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=set-up-a-team\">设置团队</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=create-a-team-task\">创建团队任务</a>。</p> <p>Enterprise 管理员通过两项权限控制谁可以创建团队和管理团队任务：<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">创建团队（Create teams）和创建与管理团队自动化（Create and manage team automations）</a>。管理员也可以将<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">工作区连接</a>提供给团队使用。每个团队的服务账户和已配置连接决定了其任务会使用哪些外部账户。</p> <p>有关团队成员管理和任务的更多信息，请参阅帮助中心的 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001541\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的团队（需联网）</a>和 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001540\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 中创建和管理团队任务（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><span id=\"plan-the-teams-access-and-responsibilities\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"how-teams-and-team-tasks-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">团队和团队任务的工作方式</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">工作区连接</a>允许团队任务使用公司管理的应用账户，因此团队成员不必各自连接自己的账户。</p> <p>团队可以由同一部门或不同职能部门中、具有共同目标的成员组成。ChatGPT 团队与<a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c?anchor=compare-membership-sources\">手动创建或通过 SCIM 同步的工作区群组</a>相互独立。</p> <p>以下是一些定时触发和事件触发团队任务的示例：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>团队</strong></th> <th><strong>协作成员</strong></th> <th><strong>团队任务示例</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>产品发布</td> <td>准备产品发布的产品、营销和支持团队。</td> <td>发布 Slack 频道收到消息时，汇总发布进度、里程碑变化和阻碍事项。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>客户成功</td> <td>为客户提供支持的客户经理和客户成功团队。</td> <td>每周一汇总上一周的客户更新、后续跟进事项和未解决问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>销售</td> <td>负责成交和客户入职的销售、解决方案工程师和客户成功团队。</td> <td>交易完成时，准备一份客户入职简报，列出客户目标、承诺事项和待解决问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>营销</td> <td>负责共同项目的项目负责人和参与者。</td> <td>每天早上汇总项目进度、阻碍事项和即将到来的截止日期。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>团队任务在云端使用团队的服务账户和已配置的应用连接运行。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">开始前</h3> <p>设置团队或团队任务之前，工作区所有者应通过工作区设置或自定义角色，为指定用户启用以下权限：</p> <ul> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">创建团队</a>：创建团队所需的权限。</p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">创建和管理团队任务</a>：创建或编辑团队任务所需的权限。</p> </li> </ul> <p>请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">角色与工作区权限</a>。</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>工作区管理员：</strong> 设置并授权获准使用的工作区连接，并选择哪些人可以发现和使用这些连接。检查外部账户的数据访问权限和操作权限。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">工作区连接</a>。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>团队所有者：</strong> 创建团队后，在权限允许的范围内选择团队需要的可用连接。安排团队任务之前，请确认每项连接使用哪个外部账户。</p> </li> </ul> <p><span id=\"2-configure-membership-and-assign-maintainers\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"set-up-a-team\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">设置团队</h3> <ol> <li> <p><strong>创建团队。</strong> 在目标工作区中，打开 Settings（设置）&gt; Teams（团队），然后选择 Create team（创建团队）。输入 Name（名称）和可选的 Description（描述），再选择 Create（创建）。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>检查访问权限并邀请同事。</strong> 邀请同事前，请检查他们是否能访问之前的运行记录和生成的文件；单项任务和单次运行不能设置单独的访问限制。选择 Invite（邀请），按 Name（姓名）或 email（电子邮箱）搜索，然后选择 Add member（添加成员）或 Add members（添加多位成员）。成员可以邀请同事，并移除非所有者成员。同一工作区内的成员可以通过加入链接直接加入，无需所有者批准。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>添加团队连接。</strong> 工作区连接使用集中管理的账户；团队连接则会与团队共享某个成员单独连接的账户。作为团队所有者，请选择你获准使用的连接。检查该连接的数据访问权限和操作权限，并在安排无人值守工作前完成任何必要的登录。拥有团队所有权并不会因此获得工作区管理员权限。管理员设置方法请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">工作区连接</a>。</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"create-and-validate-the-first-team-task\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"2-review-the-schedule-actions-and-audience\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"3-validate-access-and-the-first-result\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"create-a-team-task\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">创建团队任务</h3> <ol> <li> <p>打开 <strong>Scheduled（已安排）</strong> &gt; <strong>+ New Task（+ 新建任务）</strong>。选择 <strong>Team toggle（团队切换开关）</strong>，以及负责此任务的团队。</p> </li> <li> <p>选择 <strong>Trigger（触发器）</strong>。选择 <strong>Schedule（定时）</strong> 时，请检查时间和时区。如果选择受支持的事件触发器，请检查其触发条件和所需连接。</p> </li> <li> <p>在 <strong>Instructions（指示）</strong> 中说明目标和预期结果，包括成功标准和约束条件。添加任务专属的信息源；如果团队指定了 <a href=\"#/article/a-9eaf251f273c9bc9\">Space</a>，请一并检查共享指示。任务不会继承创建者的个人记忆、自定义指示或聊天历史。</p> </li> <li> <p>检查 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong> 和 <strong>Advanced（高级）</strong> 设置，包括 <strong>Model（模型）</strong>。选择团队可用的模型；它可能与你个人账户可用的模型不同。选择 <strong>Create（创建）</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>选择 <strong>Run now（立即运行）</strong>，并在 <strong>Previous runs（以往运行）</strong> 中检查结果。使用 <strong>Edit（编辑）</strong> 修改指示或设置。</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"review-membership-connections-and-destinations\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"handle-departures-and-stop-work-when-needed\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"teams-and-team-tasks-faq\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">团队和团队任务常见问题</h2> <p><a id=\"slackmicrosoft-teams\"></a> <strong>能否导入团队成员，或让成员与工作区群组、Slack/Microsoft Teams 频道保持同步？</strong></p> <p>不能。ChatGPT 团队成员与工作区群组、Slack 或 Microsoft Teams 频道相互独立，不能导入或同步。请在 ChatGPT 中添加或移除成员。</p> <p><strong>谁可以创建团队、更改团队成员并管理团队任务？</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">工作区权限</a>控制团队创建、团队任务创建及更新。创建团队的人会成为团队所有者，但不会因此获得工作区管理员权限。成员可以邀请同事并移除非所有者成员；同一工作区内的加入链接无需所有者批准。</p> <p>只有团队所有者可以删除团队。工作区管理员负责管理获准的连接以及连接的使用对象。</p> <p><a id=\"-1\"></a> <strong>这些工作区控制会覆盖所有受支持的团队和任务创建、编辑入口吗？</strong></p> <p>会。“创建团队”权限控制团队创建；“创建和管理团队自动化”权限控制所有受支持入口中的任务创建和更新。团队成员资格和连接权限仍然适用。</p> <p><a id=\"-2\"></a> <strong>加入团队后会获得哪些访问权限？</strong></p> <p>新成员可以查看所有以前的运行记录和生成的文件；单项任务和单次运行不能设置单独的访问限制。<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=share-a-page-or-space\">Pages 和 Spaces 仍有各自的分享权限</a>。加入团队后，你也会获得共享给该团队的页面和空间的访问权限。加入团队不会分享个人聊天或连接。工作区成员打开加入链接时，可以在加入前查看团队名称和成员列表。</p> <p><a id=\"-3\"></a> <strong>工作区管理员不加入团队，也能如何检查活动？</strong></p> <p>管理员可以通过 <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=get-started\">Compliance API</a>检查活动，并按角色限制访问。</p> <p><a id=\"-4\"></a> <strong>团队任务使用谁的账户？</strong></p> <p>团队任务使用团队的服务账户和<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=understand-the-connected-accounts-permissions\">已配置的应用连接</a>。连接所用的账户决定其数据访问范围和操作权限；这些权限可能不同于创建者或编辑者个人账户的权限。请参阅帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">连接和管理应用账户（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"-5\"></a> <strong>插件和连接如何配合使用？</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=connections-for-teams-and-workflows\">团队插件和连接</a>用途不同：插件提供工具或技能；连接提供应用访问权限。成员不必分别连接同一个账户。</p> <p><a id=\"-6\"></a> <strong>工作区连接是否可能访问超出成员个人权限范围的信息？</strong></p> <p>可能。已连接账户能够访问成员个人账户无法访问的信息。请同时检查团队成员资格和每项连接可以访问的资源。</p> <p><a id=\"-7\"></a> <strong>团队任务能否向已连接的系统写入数据？</strong></p> <p>可以，但前提是工具和连接都允许这样做，例如向 Slack 发帖。无人值守运行无法完成新的应用登录，并且仍受操作审批要求约束。</p> <p><a id=\"-8\"></a> <strong>任务创建者或团队所有者离开后会怎样？</strong></p> <p>获准的团队成员可以编辑、暂停或恢复共享任务。<a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c?anchor=remove-a-departing-employee\">为即将离职的创建者或所有者办理离职流程</a>之前，请检查团队所有权和所需连接。</p> <p>团队任务旨在让创建者离开后仍能继续运行，但所需连接可能会失去访问权限。</p> <p>所有者离开前必须转移所有权。新所有者无法访问的连接会对整个团队停用。</p> <p><a id=\"-9\"></a> <strong>暂停或删除任务后，正在运行和排队中的任务会怎样？</strong></p> <p>暂停任务会阻止之后的定时运行和事件触发运行。不要依赖暂停或删除任务来中断已经开始的运行。</p> <p><a id=\"-10\"></a> <strong>管理员可以审计哪些团队和任务活动？</strong></p> <p>团队的 <strong>Activity（活动）</strong> 视图会记录更改。获准的成员可以检查单次运行及其结果。</p> <p>调查团队活动时，请使用受支持的 <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=confirm-the-administration-boundaries\">Compliance API</a>记录。依赖这些记录进行审计前，请确认哪些团队、任务和连接记录可用。</p> <p>每项事件的准确字段和支持范围，请使用最新的 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API 参考（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"-11\"></a> <strong>团队任务如何计费？</strong></p> <p>团队任务使用工作区额度。团队支出限额与用户限额相互独立。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"set-up-and-manage-teams-and-team-tasks\">Set up and manage teams and Team Tasks</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Teams give people in ChatGPT a shared place to organize work and collaborate. With Team Tasks, members can set up work to run on a schedule or when a specific event occurs, such as preparing a weekly report or summarizing new project updates.</p> <p>To get started, learn how to <a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=set-up-a-team\">set up a team</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=create-a-team-task\">create a Team Task</a>.</p> <p>Enterprise admins control who can create teams and manage Team Tasks through two permissions: <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">Create teams and Create and manage team automations</a>. Admins can also make <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">workspace connections</a> available to teams. Each team’s service account and configured connections determine which external accounts its tasks use.</p> <p>For more on team membership and tasks, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001541\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Teams in ChatGPT (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001540\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and managing team tasks in ChatGPT (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <p><span id=\"plan-the-teams-access-and-responsibilities\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"how-teams-and-team-tasks-work\">How teams and Team Tasks work</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">Workspace connections</a> let Team Tasks use company-managed app accounts so each team member doesn't need to connect their own account.</p> <p>Teams can include people within a department or across functions who share a goal. A team in ChatGPT is separate from a <a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c?anchor=compare-membership-sources\">workspace group created manually or synced through SCIM</a>.</p> <p>Here are examples of scheduled and event-triggered Team Tasks:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>Team</strong></th> <th><strong>Who works together</strong></th> <th><strong>Example Team Task</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Product launch</td> <td>Product, marketing, and support teams preparing a release.</td> <td>When a message arrives in the launch Slack channel, summarize launch progress, milestone changes, and blockers.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Customer success</td> <td>Account managers and customer success teams supporting customers.</td> <td>Each Monday, summarize the previous week's customer updates, follow-ups and open questions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Sales</td> <td>Sales, solutions engineers, and customer success teams closing deals and onboarding customers</td> <td>When a deal closes, prepare an onboarding brief with customer goals, commitments, and open questions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Marketing</td> <td>Project leads and contributors responsible for a shared project.</td> <td>Each morning, summarize project progress, blockers, and upcoming deadlines.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Team Tasks run in the cloud with the team's service account and configured app connections.</p> <h3 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h3> <p>Before setting up a team or its tasks, a workspace owner should enable the following permissions for the intended users through workspace settings or custom roles:</p> <ul> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">Create teams</a>: Required to create a team</p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">Create and manage team tasks</a>: Required to create or edit team tasks</p> </li> </ul> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">Roles and workspace permissions</a>.</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>Workspace admin:</strong> Set up and authorize approved workspace connections, and choose who can find and use them. Check the external account’s data and action permissions. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">Workspace connections</a>.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Team owner:</strong> After creating the team, select the available connections it needs where your permissions allow. Before scheduling a Team Task, confirm which external account each connection uses.</p> </li> </ul> <p><span id=\"2-configure-membership-and-assign-maintainers\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"set-up-a-team\">Set up a team</h3> <ol> <li> <p><strong>Create the team</strong>. In the intended workspace, open Settings &gt; Teams and select Create team. Enter a Name and optional Description, then select Create.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Review access and invite colleagues</strong>. Before inviting colleagues, review access to earlier runs and generated files; individual tasks and runs cannot have separate access restrictions. Select Invite, search by Name or email, and select Add member or Add members. Members can invite coworkers and remove non-owner members. Same-workspace join links do not require owner approval.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Add the team’s connections.</strong> Workspace connections use centrally managed accounts; team connections share an individually connected account with the team. As team owner, choose a connection you’re allowed to use. Review its data and action permissions, and complete any required sign-in before unattended work. Team ownership doesn’t grant workspace admin permissions. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">Workspace connections</a> for admin setup.</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"create-and-validate-the-first-team-task\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"2-review-the-schedule-actions-and-audience\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"3-validate-access-and-the-first-result\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"create-a-team-task\">Create a Team Task</h3> <ol> <li> <p>Open <strong>Scheduled</strong> &gt; <strong>+ New Task</strong>. Select the <strong>Team toggle</strong> and the team that will own the task.</p> </li> <li> <p>Choose a <strong>Trigger</strong>. For <strong>Schedule</strong>, check the timing and time zone. For a supported event trigger, check its conditions and required connection.</p> </li> <li> <p>In <strong>Instructions</strong>, describe the goal and expected output. Include success criteria and guardrails. Link task-specific sources, and review shared instructions if the team has a designated <a href=\"#/article/a-9eaf251f273c9bc9\">Space</a>. Tasks do not inherit the creator’s personal memories, custom instructions, or chat history.</p> </li> <li> <p>Review <strong>Plugins</strong> and <strong>Advanced</strong> settings, including <strong>Model</strong>. Choose a model available to the team; this may differ from your personal account. Select <strong>Create</strong>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Select <strong>Run now</strong> and inspect the result in <strong>Previous runs</strong>. Use <strong>Edit</strong> to change instructions or settings.</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"review-membership-connections-and-destinations\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"handle-departures-and-stop-work-when-needed\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"teams-and-team-tasks-faq\">Teams and Team Tasks FAQ</h2> <p><a id=\"can-team-membership-be-imported-or-kept-in-sync-with-workspace-groups-or-slackmicrosoft-teams-channels\"></a> <strong>Can team membership be imported or kept in sync with workspace groups or Slack/Microsoft Teams channels?</strong></p> <p>No. ChatGPT team membership is separate from workspace groups and Slack or Microsoft Teams channels. It cannot be imported or synced; add and remove members in ChatGPT.</p> <p><a id=\"who-can-create-a-team-change-its-membership-and-manage-its-tasks\"></a> <strong>Who can create a team, change its membership, and manage its tasks?</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">Workspace permissions</a> control team creation and task creation or updates. The creator becomes team owner without gaining workspace admin rights. Members can invite coworkers and remove non-owner members; same-workspace join links need no owner approval.</p> <p>Only the team owner can delete the team. Workspace admins manage approved connections and who can use them.</p> <p><a id=\"are-these-workspace-controls-enforced-across-every-supported-team-and-task-creation-or-editing-entry-point\"></a> <strong>Are these workspace controls enforced across every supported team and task creation or editing entry point?</strong></p> <p>Yes. Create teams governs team creation; Create and manage team automations governs task creation and updates across supported entry points. Team membership and connection permissions still apply.</p> <p><a id=\"what-access-does-someone-gain-when-they-join-a-team\"></a> <strong>What access does someone gain when they join a team?</strong></p> <p>New members can see all earlier runs and generated files; individual tasks and runs cannot have separate access restrictions. <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=share-a-page-or-space\">Pages and Spaces retain their own sharing permissions</a>. Joining a team, you’ll inherit any pages and spaces that are shared with the team. Joining does not share personal chats or connections. Workspace members opening a join link can see the team’s name and member list before joining.</p> <p><a id=\"how-can-workspace-admins-review-activity-without-joining-a-team\"></a> <strong>How can workspace admins review activity without joining a team?</strong></p> <p>Admins can review activity through the <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=get-started\">Compliance API</a> and restrict access by role.</p> <p><a id=\"whose-account-does-a-team-task-use\"></a> <strong>Whose account does a Team Task use?</strong></p> <p>Team Tasks use the team’s service account and <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=understand-the-connected-accounts-permissions\">configured app connections</a>. A connection’s account determines its data and actions, which may differ from the creator’s or editor’s personal access. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Connecting and managing app accounts (online)</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"how-do-plugins-and-connections-work-together\"></a> <strong>How do plugins and connections work together?</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=connections-for-teams-and-workflows\">Team plugins and connections</a> serve different purposes: plugins provide tools or skills; connections supply app access. Members need not connect the same account individually.</p> <p><a id=\"can-workspace-connections-expose-information-beyond-a-memberx27s-personal-access\"></a> <strong>Can workspace connections expose information beyond a member's personal access?</strong></p> <p>Yes. Connected accounts may access information a member’s own account cannot. Review team membership alongside each connection’s resource access.</p> <p><a id=\"can-team-tasks-write-to-connected-systems\"></a> <strong>Can Team Tasks write to connected systems?</strong></p> <p>Yes, if the tool and connection allow it—for example, posting to Slack. Unattended runs cannot complete a new app sign-in and remain subject to action-approval requirements.</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-when-a-task-creator-or-team-owner-leaves\"></a> <strong>What happens when a task creator or team owner leaves?</strong></p> <p>Authorized teammates can edit, pause, or resume shared tasks. Before <a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c?anchor=remove-a-departing-employee\">offboarding a creator or owner</a>, review team ownership and required connections.</p> <p>Team-owned tasks are designed to persist after the creator leaves, but required connections may lose access.</p> <p>Owners must transfer ownership before leaving. Connections the new owner cannot access become disabled for the entire team.</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-to-active-and-queued-runs-when-a-task-is-paused-or-deleted\"></a> <strong>What happens to active and queued runs when a task is paused or deleted?</strong></p> <p>Pausing prevents future scheduled and event-triggered runs. Neither pausing nor deleting a task should be relied on to interrupt an active run.</p> <p><a id=\"what-team-and-task-activity-can-admins-audit\"></a> <strong>What team and task activity can admins audit?</strong></p> <p>The team’s Activity view keeps track of changes. Authorized members can inspect individual runs and results.</p> <p>Use supported <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=confirm-the-administration-boundaries\">Compliance API</a> records to investigate team activity. Confirm which team, task, and connection records are available before relying on them for an audit.</p> <p>Use the current <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a> for each event’s exact fields and supported coverage.</p> <p><a id=\"how-are-team-tasks-billed\"></a> <strong>How are Team Tasks billed?</strong></p> <p>Team Tasks use workspace credits. Team spending limits are separate from user limits.</p>"};
